There is a textile merchant and a woman selling felafels.	這裡有一位布商，還有一名賣法拉費的婦人。
The woman sells her felafels, but as I suspected, Ibrahim has forsaken his business for the pleasure of his wife's company. And who can blame him?	那婦人一如往常做著生意，但正如我所料，易布拉興撇下了鋪子，只顧著陪伴愛妻。這又能怪他嗎？
It is golden fried and hot from oil. You must either eat it or give it to someone, Arthur. It will crumble to bits if you carry it about.	它炸得金黃，帶著油鍋的熱氣。你得立刻吃掉，或轉手給人，亞瑟。若一直帶在身上，它會碎成渣。
You were warned they are delicate. It has crumbled away to nothing.	早提醒過你這東西易碎。它已經碎成渣，什麼都不剩了。
There is a basket of crisp, golden brown felafels, fresh from the oil on the woman's table.	婦人的攤桌上，有一籃酥脆金黃、剛出油鍋的法拉費。
It is dark and empty.	裡頭又暗又空。
He has quite a lot of it.	他這東西可不少。
There is a basket of raw felafel balls and a basket of fried felafels.	這裡有一籃生的法拉費丸子，還有一籃炸好的法拉費。
It looks uninviting.	看起來讓人提不起食慾。
Your mule is across the street with the weapons merchant.	你的騾子在街對面，跟武器商在一起。
How?	怎麼做？
The felafels do smell especially good.	這些法拉費聞起來確實格外香。
Nay, do not disturb Ibrahim and his wife at such a moment.	不可，此刻不該打擾易布拉興夫婦。
If Ibrahim wanted you to enter, he would invite you.	若易布拉興想讓你進去，他自會邀你入內。
Ibrahim has not returned.	易布拉興還沒回來。
I do not think you will see Ibrahim any time soon.	我想你一時半刻是見不著易布拉興了。
No need to stand there drooling. Help yourself, I said.	用不著站在那裡流口水。我說了，自己拿去吃吧。
He has rather a taste for bright colours, I note.	我注意到，他挺偏愛鮮豔的色彩。
The textile merchant has quite an array of cloth.	這位布商陳列著各式各樣的布料。
You cannot see through the door.	你透過門看不進去。
Observe, if you will, the quality of my fabrics. You will find none finer even if you journeyed to Constantinople, and indeed, some have come from twice as far.	且請細看，我這些布料的品質。縱使你遠赴君士坦丁堡，也找不到更好的了——其中有些，來歷還遠上一倍不止。
See the exquisite colors, the glowing patterns, the perfect weave of these silks from the Orient.	瞧瞧這些東方絲綢，色澤精緻、紋樣鮮亮、織工完美無瑕。
And these magnificent linens that will keep you cool when the sun scorches the earth, and by its virtue of absorbing moisture, will keep you dry.	還有這些上等亞麻布，烈日炙烤大地時能為你消暑，又因其吸濕之性，能讓你保持乾爽。
Then perhaps you come from a colder clime, as indeed your armor would hint. See my beautifully dyed woolens and feel the perfection of their natural oils.	那麼，你或許來自較寒冷之地——你這身盔甲確實透著這樣的訊息。瞧瞧我這染色精美的羊毛織品，感受一下它天然油脂的極致觸感。
You are undoubtedly awed by the selection. Take your time.	你想必是被這些選擇給看呆了。慢慢挑吧。
My anguish overwhelms me. I cannot speak.	我痛苦難當，說不出話來。
But you are not buying anything.	但你什麼都沒買。
Keep it away! I once had a mule who ate cloth. I will never keep one again.	拿開！我曾養過一頭吃布的騾子，此後再也不敢養了。
Ahh! You have it, habibi! If only I could have it, I would be the happiest man in the world!	啊！你竟然有這個，朋友！我若能擁有它，便是世上最快樂的人了！
No thank you. I do not eat meat.	不用了，謝謝。我不吃肉。
Forgive my ingratitude, but I have eaten more of Sarah's felafels than the sky has stars.	恕我失禮，莎拉的法拉費，我吃過的怕是比天上的星星還多。
You wish me to accept this gift? I cannot imagine why. I must respectfully decline.	你要我收下這份禮？我實在想不出理由。恕我不能領受。
No, I do not eat meat.	不，我不吃肉。
I think not today, thank you. May Allah guide you elsewhere.	今日就不必了，多謝。願阿拉指引你前往別處。
Rather ostentatious for you, I deem, and not of much use without the skills of a tailor.	依我看，這對你來說未免太招搖，何況沒有裁縫的手藝，也派不上什麼用場。
If you wish, here it is.	你若想要，這就給你。
Do not mention the word veil to me! It is a word of misery.	休再提「面紗」這個詞！那是個令人痛苦的字眼。
She is beautiful and trusting. I fear I do not deserve such a good wife.	她美麗又信任於我。我恐怕配不上這樣一位賢妻。
I do not have rugs for sale.	我這裡沒有地毯可賣。
Perhaps Ismail the relic merchant can help you.	或許聖物商艾思美能幫上你。
I do not know him.	我不認識他。
Just feel the marvelous fabric, habib. They can make a pauper look like a prince!	摸摸這絕妙的布料吧，朋友。它能讓乞丐看起來像王子！
My woolens are the finest in Jerusalem.	我這羊毛織品，是耶路撒冷最上乘的。
The silks come from the Orient, very rare and very beautiful.	這些絲綢來自東方，極為稀有，也極為美麗。
Yes, they plague and the city guards seldom catch them. For this, I pay taxes?	是啊，他們四處為害，城衛卻鮮少抓到他們。我繳稅就是為了這個？
That alley goes nowhere and is most unpleasant.	那條巷子哪裡都通不了，而且十分不宜久留。
Do not speak her cursed name! I wish I had never seen her!	休提她那受詛咒的名字！我真希望自己從未見過她！
My neighbor, Sarah, sells excellent felafels.	我的鄰居莎拉，賣的法拉費十分出色。
Her felafels are the best in Jerusalem.	她的法拉費是耶路撒冷最好的。
It means cloth, of course.	那當然是指布料。
The thieves are a dreadful nuisance.	那些竊賊實在是個大麻煩。
Even if you travelled there, you would find no finer fabrics than mine.	縱使你親自遠行至彼處，也找不到比我這裡更好的布料。
What can I say about that, habibi.	這事我還能說什麼呢，朋友。
It appears she partakes liberally of her own food.	看來她自己也毫不吝於享用自家的食物。
It is a heavy metal cauldron filled with bubbling hot oil.	這是口沉重的金屬大鍋，裝滿了滾沸的熱油。
One basket of raw felafels and one basket of cooked felafels sits on the table.	桌上擺著一籃生的法拉費，還有一籃煮熟的法拉費。
Stop that, Arthur. You have been away from Gwenhyver for too long.	住手，亞瑟。你離開昆海兒身邊太久了。
I see no girl, only the matronly felafel seller.	我沒看見什麼姑娘，只有那位賣法拉費的婦人。
'Tis no more than a little stall with a canopy to keep out the rain and sun, a cauldron of bubbling oil and the felafels, raw and cooked.	不過是個小攤子，撐著遮風擋雨的棚子，一口滾油的大鍋，還有生的、熟的法拉費。
Ah, it is you! How good to see your face again. If you want a felafel, just speak up.	啊，是你！能再見到你，真是高興。想要法拉費，儘管開口。
Fresh, hot felafels for a hungry man. Made from the finest ground chick peas and ground sesame seed. Flavored with parsley, onion and garlic.	新鮮熱騰的法拉費，正合飢腸轆轆的漢子。用最上等的鷹嘴豆磨粉、芝麻磨粉製成，佐以荷蘭芹、洋蔥與大蒜調味。
Golden fried felafels cooked in pure sesame oil. If you are hungry, a felafel would work wonders for your belly. See what it has done for mine!	用純芝麻油炸得金黃的法拉費。你若餓了，一份法拉費會讓你的肚子大為滿足。瞧瞧它把我的肚子養成什麼樣子！
Well, I should not be telling you this, but all day long I cook felafels. Every day I eat felafels. Not that they are not delicious!	唉，我實在不該說這個，但我整天都在煮法拉費，天天也都在吃法拉費。倒不是它不好吃！
But even I am tired of felafels. I dream of lamb! A nice, fresh cut of lamb. Lamb and felafel! Oi, that would be Paradise.	但就連我，也吃膩了法拉費。我夢想著羊肉！一塊上好新鮮的羊肉。羊肉配法拉費！啊，那簡直是天堂。
I do not mind paying his prices, but I am terrified of the meat merchant, that evil-tempered ox! That is why I go without lamb.	他的價錢我倒不介意，可我怕透了那賣肉的，那頭脾氣暴躁的蠻牛！所以我才一直沒吃上羊肉。
Do not try to cheat me now! No coin, no felafel.	休想耍花招！沒錢就沒法拉費。
You can carry no more felafels without making a mess of yourself.	你身上帶的法拉費已經夠多了，再拿只會弄得一團糟。
They are not very good uncooked.	沒煮熟的可不怎麼好吃。
Only 1 fals for one of my delicious felafels.	我這美味的法拉費，一份只要一枚銅幣。
Gluttony is what the Christians call one of the Seven Deadly Sins, you know. That is quite enough with the felafels already.	你知道嗎，貪食是基督徒口中的七宗罪之一。法拉費就吃到這裡吧，夠了。
I rather doubt she would wish to part with that.	我很懷疑她會捨得割捨那個。
I have been craving a bit of lamb. Thank you for bringing it.	我一直饞著想吃點羊肉呢。多謝你帶來。
Why are you asking ME?	你為何問我？
That would be like giving wool to the sheep, do you not think?	那豈不是像把羊毛送給羊，你不覺得嗎？
I have no room for it, thank you all the same.	我沒地方放這個，但還是謝謝你。
Really, you are too kind, but I could not take it.	真的，你太客氣了，但我不能收下。
Very pretty. Maybe my neighbor, Ibrahim, would be interested.	真漂亮。或許我的鄰居易布拉興會有興趣。
What, do I look rich?	怎麼，我看起來像是有錢人嗎？
Buy another one, if you please.	勞煩再買一份吧。
You mean like a cup? Farabi across the street sells cups.	你是說像杯子那樣的東西？街對面的法拉比有賣杯子。
Galahad? What a strange name.	葛拉漢？好奇怪的名字。
I am cooking felafels, of course.	我當然是在煮法拉費。
He simply appeared days ago and never says a word. An orphan, no doubt.	他就這麼幾天前冒出來的，一句話也不說。想必是個孤兒。
I use very fine ingredients in my felafels.	我的法拉費用的都是上等食材。
I cook the felafels in my cauldron, until they are just right.	我在鍋裡煮法拉費，煮到恰到好處為止。
He knows cloth well, but he has much to learn about women.	他對布料很懂，但論起女人，他還有得學。
I cannot help you with that.	這事我幫不上忙。
Help yourself.	自己拿去吧。
But you must eat it quickly or it will crumble. My felafels are as delicate as they are delicious.	但你得快點吃，不然它會碎掉。我的法拉費，好吃歸好吃，卻也一樣易碎。
I can sense how much you enjoyed that crisp, hot felafel.	我看得出來，你有多喜歡那份酥脆熱燙的法拉費。
I fail to see how you could have enjoyed that with the eyes of that poor hungry urchin upon you.	那可憐飢餓的流浪孩子盯著你看，我實在不懂你怎麼吃得下去。
Under Sarah's care, he will be happy and healthy. Right you are to feel proud of this deed.	在莎拉的照料下，他會過得快樂又健康。你為此感到自豪，是應該的。
He is only a young boy, a half-starved, ragged urchin who is surely alone in the world. What a pathetic sight!	他不過是個小男孩，半飢半飽、衣衫襤褸，想必在這世上孤苦無依。多麼可憐的景象！
You will need to move closer to the boy, but gently! He is alone and afraid.	你得再靠近那孩子一些，但要輕柔！他孤單又害怕。
One of your felafels is reduced to crumbs from too much handling.	你有一份法拉費，因為拿太久，已經碎成渣了。
Your only felafel is reduced to crumbs from too much handling.	你僅剩的那份法拉費，因為拿太久，已經碎成渣了。
Of the Arab and Hebrew writing, I can tell you nothing, but the Latin is easy: "fictilia" refers to pottery, "cetarius" means fishmonger, and "horreum" is a granary.	阿拉伯文與希伯來文的部分，我一無所知，但拉丁文倒是簡單：「fictilia」指陶器，「cetarius」指魚販，「horreum」則是穀倉。
Across the street are three merchants.	街對面有三位商人。
There is a merchant selling pottery, a fishmonger and a grain merchant.	這裡有一位賣陶器的商人、一位魚販，還有一位穀物商。
The birds are perched upon the arch.	鳥兒棲在拱門上。
Aye, there are birds pecking at dropped grain. Nothing unusual about that.	正是，有幾隻鳥在啄食掉落的穀粒，沒什麼稀奇的。
You have startled the birds and sent them flying.	你驚動了那些鳥，牠們都飛走了。
It is a pottery shop, though he undoubtedly deals in more than mere ceramics.	這是間陶器店，不過他做的生意想必不只陶器。
It is a fishmonger's shop.	這是間魚舖。
It is a granary.	這是座穀倉。
The only symbol I see is a stalk of grain on the horreum.	我只看得出一個符號——穀倉上的一株麥穗。
Looks like a sleek, well-fed cat with a taste for fish.	看起來是隻毛色油亮、養得肥胖的貓，愛吃魚。
I cannot say what fish they are, but they smell bad enough.	我說不出那是什麼魚，但氣味已經夠難聞了。
The fragrant herbs have certainly improved this part of the bazaar.	這些香草，確實讓市集這一帶好聞了不少。
The restless grain merchant has huge jars presumably filled with grain.	那位坐立難安的穀物商，擺著幾個大罐子，想必裝的都是穀物。
The huge clay jars are filled with grain.	這些大陶罐裡裝滿了穀物。
He is a most agitated man.	他是個十分焦躁不安的人。
The birds are happy as they are. Leave them alone.	鳥兒就這樣挺自在的，別去打擾牠們。
The scents from the fishmonger's stall are vastly improved.	魚販攤子傳來的氣味，已經好聞許多。
The smell of the fishmonger's wares is an assault to the nose.	魚販貨品的氣味，簡直是對鼻子的一種侵犯。
The grain merchant will not stop pacing. He is a most agitated man.	那位穀物商踱步不停，是個十分焦躁不安的人。
He is the fattest merchant I have ever seen.	他是我見過最胖的商人。
The pottery he has on display outside his shop is really quite plain, more for function than pleasure, I would say.	他店外陳列的陶器相當樸素，依我看，重實用而不重美觀。
He has a number of earthenware jars on display.	他陳列著不少陶罐。
His shelves display plain, but well-made pieces of pottery. Probably only his least valuable wares, considering the problem with thieves.	他架上擺的陶器樸素卻做工紮實。考慮到竊賊猖獗，這些想必只是他最不值錢的貨色。
Welcome back. Let me know if I may serve you.	歡迎回來。若有什麼能為你效勞的，儘管開口。
I have but two wishes in the world. One is that the wind which blows down this street will not change, so that the smell of fish stays away from my shop.	我在這世上只有兩個願望。其一，是這街上吹的風永遠別變向，好讓魚腥味遠離我的鋪子。
And the other? Why, to sell you something. A mug or bowl of earthenware perhaps. Inside, under lock and key, I have fine silver plates and goblets. I have a few other items, probably of no interest to you, such as mirrors.	另一個？當然是賣你點東西。或許一只陶杯或陶碗？我店裡上鎖收著的，還有上好的銀盤與高腳杯。此外也有些別的物件，你大概不感興趣，比如鏡子。
Please speak if there is anything I might sell you.	若有什麼想買的，儘管開口。
Be not misled by my sign, habib. True, I deal in earthenware -- bowls and plates and jugs and vases for everyday use, but I have richer wares which are not safe to display on this street.	莫被我的招牌給誤導了，朋友。沒錯，我是賣陶器——日常用的碗、盤、罐、瓶，但我還有更貴重的貨色，在這條街上可不敢公然陳列。
I have silver plates, bowls, goblets. Plain or worked with design. Shined to glimmering perfection. I sell mirrors as well.	我有銀盤、銀碗、高腳杯，素面的或雕花的都有，擦得光亮閃耀。我也賣鏡子。
Even gold plates and goblets I can make to order, if your wealth is great enough. Plain or patterned or encrusted with jewels.	就連金盤與金杯，我也能訂製——只要你財力夠雄厚。素面的、雕花的，或鑲滿寶石的，皆可。
I am at your service when you know what you want...and can show the coin for it.	等你想清楚要買什麼……又拿得出錢來，我隨時恭候。
No coin, no sale.	沒錢就沒生意。
I am not sure what you wish to buy.	我不確定你想買什麼。
